---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "~/config/site";

const lastUpdated = "23 April 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Cookies"
  description={`${site.legalName} cookie and tracking notice.`}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5">Cookie and tracking notice</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-moss text-[0.9rem]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="maz-prose mt-10">
        <p>
          This notice explains how {site.legalName} uses cookies and similar
          technologies on <a href={site.url}>{site.url}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          {site.legalName}, trading as {site.brand}, is registered in England
          and Wales under company number {site.legal.companyNumber}. Its
          registered office is {site.legal.registeredAddress}.
        </p>

        <h2>What cookies are</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a
          website. Similar technologies include pixels, tags, scripts, local
          storage and SDK-style identifiers used to recognise a browser or
          device, remember preferences, measure activity and support marketing.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>Depending on the page, campaign and tools active on the site, we may use cookies and similar technologies for:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>essential site functionality and security;</li>
          <li>traffic measurement, analytics and site improvement;</li>
          <li>campaign attribution and conversion measurement;</li>
          <li>remarketing and advertising audience creation;</li>
          <li>newsletter, CRM or lead-source tracking linked to forms and campaigns.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Categories of cookies</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Strictly necessary:</strong> help core site functions,
            security and load balancing work properly.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics and performance:</strong> help us understand how
            visitors use the site so we can improve journeys, content and
            conversion performance.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising and remarketing:</strong> used by marketing
            partners such as Google and Meta to measure ad performance, build
            audiences and show more relevant advertising.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Functional:</strong> support embedded services such as
            scheduling tools, video tools or lead-capture experiences.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Third-party tools we may use</h2>
        <p>
          Our marketing and website stack may include tools such as Calendly,
          Google Analytics, Google Ads, Meta advertising technologies, CRM and
          newsletter tools, and other measurement or marketing services we use
          from time to time. These providers may collect information directly
          from your device or browser when their scripts, pixels or embeds are
          loaded.
        </p>

        <h2>Consent and control</h2>
        <p>
          Where required by law, non-essential cookies and similar technologies
          should only be used with appropriate choice or consent. You can also
          manage cookies through your browser settings, device settings, ad
          platform controls and any consent tools we make available on the
          website.
        </p>
        <p>
          Please note that disabling certain cookies may affect how parts of
          the site, embedded tools or marketing journeys work.
        </p>

        <h2>How long cookies last</h2>
        <p>
          Some cookies are session-based and expire when you close your
          browser. Others remain for a defined period unless you delete them
          earlier. Retention varies by provider and platform configuration.
        </p>

        <h2>Targeted advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Advertising cookies and similar technologies may be used to measure
          visits from campaigns, understand which pages or actions led to a
          booking or enquiry, and build audiences for future campaigns. In some
          jurisdictions this activity may be treated as targeted advertising or
          sharing of personal information.
        </p>

        <h2>More information</h2>
        <p>
          For more detail on how we handle personal data, see our
          <a href="/privacy"> privacy policy</a>. If you have questions about
          this notice or want to raise a privacy request, email
          <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .maz-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .maz-prose p { margin: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--color-ink); line-height: 1.7; }
  .maz-prose ul { margin: 0.75rem 0; padding-left: 1.4rem; color: var(--color-ink); line-height: 1.7; }
  .maz-prose ul li { list-style: disc; margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  .maz-prose a {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-gold);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
